  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 88f6fa2b89436164b8e97b17d82dc9a2, type: 3}
  m_Name: 19 - For Loop
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: UtilityScriptIWrite::HintSO
  hintId: tutorial_for
  isUnlockedByDefault: 0
  ignoreLock: 1
  title: For Loop
  image: {fileID: 0}
  description: 'A <font="JetBrainsMono SDF"><color=#D96DD3>for</color></font> loop
    is used to repeat instructions a specific number of times.


    A <font="JetBrainsMono
    SDF"><color=#D96DD3>for</color></font> loop commonly uses <font="JetBrainsMono
    SDF"><color=#F5F5AB>range</color>()</font> to determine how many times the loop
    should repeat.


    The letter <font="JetBrainsMono SDF">i</font> is a <color=yellow>local
    variable</color> that tracks the loop''s progress. It only exists inside the
    loop and is removed after the loop finishes. It is a standard naming convention,
    but you are free to name it anything you want!


    Example:

    <indent=1em><font="JetBrainsMono
    SDF"><color=#6A9955># Move 3 times</color></font></indent>

    <indent=1em><font="JetBrainsMono
    SDF"><color=#D96DD3>for</color> i <color=#D96DD3>in</color> <color=#F5F5AB>range</color>(<color=#B5CEA8>3</color>)<color=#D4D4D4>:</color></font></indent>

    <indent=3em><font="JetBrainsMono
    SDF"><color=#33CC66>move</color>(<color=#CE9178>"forward"</color>, <color=#B5CEA8>1</color>)</indent>


    In
    this example, <font="JetBrainsMono SDF"><color=#33CC66>move</color>()</font>
    executes 3 times.'
  isImageBig: 0
